From 396159d656a8d1065a3c3490bd60735de0237207 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: "Claude (for Kush)" <kushisthecoolest@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 26 Oct 2026 13:32:23 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 3/5] Gradle on Linux: gradlew, linux64 target, staged runtime,
 CMake bridge

- gradlew: Gradle's POSIX wrapper script for the pinned 9.3.1
  distribution. It puts gradle-wrapper.jar on the classpath and runs
  org.gradle.wrapper.GradleWrapperMain: the checked-in wrapper jar has
  no Main-Class manifest entry, so `java -jar` fails on it. The checked-in wrapper jar and properties
  (with distributionSha256Sum) are unchanged.
- On a Linux host the only target is linux64, and it is the default:
  -Parch accepts linux64 only, and the version gets the -linux64 suffix.
  Windows targets, defaults and the fat JAR are unchanged.
- stageLinuxRuntime -PlinuxRuntime=<libremix.so or dir>
  [-PlinuxDlssDir=<dir>] copies a local runtime build and the DLSS
  feature libraries into remix-runtime/linux64 and records the source
  in .local-sdk-source. By default the DLSS libraries come from the
  dxvk-remix checkout of scripts/build-runtime.sh's layout.
  fetchRuntimeSdkLinux64 only checks: there is no managed Linux runtime.
- compileNativeLinux64 builds libremixbridge.so with CMake into
  build/native/linux64, with jni.h from the JDK running Gradle.
- syncRuntimeSdk, packageJar and verifyPackageJar know the Linux file
  names: native/remix-sdk-linux64/{libremix.so, libremixbridge.so,
  libnvidia-ngx-*.so.*}.
- fetchRuntimeTextures runs Packman's POSIX entry point on Linux.
  migrateDevelopmentResourcePacks (PowerShell, Windows-only legacy
  packs) is skipped there.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01Tb41TgDi74v7sgH5LJBZ5A
Signed-off-by: Claude (for Kush) <kushisthecoolest@gmail.com>
